  "scope": "Faster decode: both lanes move to runtimes whose MTP3 verify-pass Q4/Q5 projections share each activation load across weight rows and whose Q4 gate/up kernel no longer conflicts on shared-memory banks - RTX 5090 container to 8cc0810a and RTX 4090 native Windows to 5a774841, which keeps one-row Q5 split2 kernels on the native lanes because the row pair measured slower there. On the RTX 5090 decode is 10.3-11.0% faster with outputs identical to v0.8.0's kernels; the RTX 4090's C1 decode rises from 153.54 to 157.89 tok/s (docs/measurements/2026-09-25-decode-kernel-schedules.json). The upstream OMP 18.3.0 client, model, serving settings and memory floors are unchanged from v0.8.0. RTX 3090 is omitted pending physical-host access. Every runtime gate below was measured on the published components; nothing is carried from v0.8.0.",
