  "interpretation": "Decode is faster on both lanes with unchanged behavior. On the RTX 5090 the release build behind the published image decodes 10.3-11.0% more tokens per second than v0.8.0's kernels from a seed context to 31K tokens, with byte-identical kernel outputs, identical role-corpus answers and exact 130,048-token retrieval. On the published image its 2,048-token decode gate ran 151.33 tok/s against 138.03 on v0.8.0's published image, and the durability workload, publication barrier, probe set, shared-prefix capacity and stock OMP 18.3.0 session proof reproduce v0.8.0's results. The RTX 4090 package passed its 15 canonical phases with the OMP 18.3.0 tool call and a C1 decode of 157.89 tok/s against 153.54, after a first candidate that shared loads in the Q5 split2 kernels was 2.7% slower; stock OMP kept one session across the installed lane's managed restarts. Automatic checkpoints stay best effort and universal warm reuse is not claimed; alphastorm/omp-ninfer#48 stays open until field confirmation.",
